uestion" "e-7454" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|\\det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|2\\cdot 4-3\\cdot 1| \\\\  & =|8-3| \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/example-7454.json" "file_sha256" "33ce61ff3b3eff90b73d97587fc8ed27370ec5f6d5a6c71547fc1706adcf4d0f" "basis" 1373 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5470" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/assets/e8ff769df4089e6ed9a47d56d7317acf41b8aef6a255abc705c0e7ec31a446ea.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/example-5470.json" "file_sha256" "c540f19593230c2bf66261e81290e2ad951b228377ba1f90d598d7a6d13d9518" "basis" 1373 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5470" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that for any linear transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $\\mathbf{T}(D)$ under the action of $\\mathbf{T}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(\\mathbf{T}(D)) = |\\det(T)| \\cdot \\text{Area}(D)\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D) = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4 = 6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\det(T) = 4 \\cdot 2 -  2 \\cdot (-1) = 10.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,10\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/example-5470.json" "file_sha256" "c540f19593230c2bf66261e81290e2ad951b228377ba1f90d598d7a6d13d9518" "basis" 1373 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5471" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A triangle $D$ has vertices $(1,1)$, $(4,5),$ and $(-2,1).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/example-5471.json" "file_sha256" "e74b89bed562110da2e5613f76a220037b89e7198d5f1c29d7f0ad3d7279ef43" "basis" 1373 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5471" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/assets/ee8f0cf16983d87fa505303ed6372a3f389518d05b3e13f2e9e2121038792b84.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $\\mathbf{T}(D)$ under the action of $\\mathbf{T}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(\\mathbf{T}(D)) = |\\det(T)| \\cdot \\text{Area}(D)\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D) = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4 = 6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\det(T) = (-7) \\cdot 3 -  5 \\cdot (-2) = -11.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|-11|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =66.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/example-5471.json" "file_sha256" "e74b89bed562110da2e5613f76a220037b89e7198d5f1c29d7f0ad3d7279ef43" "basis" 1373 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-316575" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $T$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}9 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\nThe area scale factor is\n{{field-1}} ." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "10db4be79b372551811e9c8057554c4c907ccad3de5d46d2c1ca5143b8686c90"} {"question" "q-316575" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|9\\cdot 1-(-4)\\cdot 2| \\\\  & =|9-(-8)| \\\\  & =17.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "10db4be79b372551811e9c8057554c4c907ccad3de5d46d2c1ca5143b8686c90"} {"question" "q-316575" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "69b0c4f1e8b87d115dd43be36f5eacfb20bc6694e6674c5d0161a16bf5892105"} {"question" "q-316575" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "10db4be79b372551811e9c8057554c4c907ccad3de5d46d2c1ca5143b8686c90"} {"question" "q-316575" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "17"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "10db4be79b372551811e9c8057554c4c907ccad3de5d46d2c1ca5143b8686c90"} {"question" "q-316571" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $T$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 10 \\\\ 8 & -1\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\nThe area scale factor is\n{{field-1}} ." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "10db4be79b372551811e9c8057554c4c907ccad3de5d46d2c1ca5143b8686c90"} {"question" "q-316571" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|3\\cdot (-1)-10\\cdot 8| \\\\  & =|-3-80| \\\\  & =|-83| \\\\  & =83.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "10db4be79b372551811e9c8057554c4c907ccad3de5d46d2c1ca5143b8686c90"} {"question" "q-316571" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "69b0c4f1e8b87d115dd43be36f5eacfb20bc6694e6674c5d0161a16bf5892105"} {"question" "q-316571" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "10db4be79b372551811e9c8057554c4c907ccad3de5d46d2c1ca5143b8686c90"} {"question" "q-316571" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "83"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "10db4be79b372551811e9c8057554c4c907ccad3de5d46d2c1ca5143b8686c90"} {"question" "q-316569" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $T$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 8\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\nThe area scale factor is\n{{field-1}} ." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "10db4be79b372551811e9c8057554c4c907ccad3de5d46d2c1ca5143b8686c90"} {"question" "q-316569" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|-10\\cdot 8-9\\cdot 1| \\\\  & =|-80-9| \\\\  & =|-89| \\\\  & =89.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "10db4be79b372551811e9c8057554c4c907ccad3de5d46d2c1ca5143b8686c90"} {"question" "q-316569" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "69b0c4f1e8b87d115dd43be36f5eacfb20bc6694e6674c5d0161a16bf5892105"} {"question" "q-316569" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "10db4be79b372551811e9c8057554c4c907ccad3de5d46d2c1ca5143b8686c90"} {"question" "q-316569" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "89"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "10db4be79b372551811e9c8057554c4c907ccad3de5d46d2c1ca5143b8686c90"} {"question" "q-84702" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $T$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 5\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "10db4be79b372551811e9c8057554c4c907ccad3de5d46d2c1ca5143b8686c90"} {"question" "q-84702" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|(-4)\\cdot 5-3\\cdot (-6)| \\\\  & =|-20+18| \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "10db4be79b372551811e9c8057554c4c907ccad3de5d46d2c1ca5143b8686c90"} {"question" "q-84702" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "69b0c4f1e8b87d115dd43be36f5eacfb20bc6694e6674c5d0161a16bf5892105"} {"question" "q-84702" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "10db4be79b372551811e9c8057554c4c907ccad3de5d46d2c1ca5143b8686c90"} {"question" "q-84702" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "18"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "20"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "10db4be79b372551811e9c8057554c4c907ccad3de5d46d2c1ca5143b8686c90"} {"question" "q-84702" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "10db4be79b372551811e9c8057554c4c907ccad3de5d46d2c1ca5143b8686c90"} {"question" "q-316573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $T$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -5\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\nThe area scale factor is\n{{field-1}} ." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "10db4be79b372551811e9c8057554c4c907ccad3de5d46d2c1ca5143b8686c90"} {"question" "q-316573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|-6\\cdot (-5)-1\\cdot (-4)| \\\\  & =|30-(-4)| \\\\  & =34.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "10db4be79b372551811e9c8057554c4c907ccad3de5d46d2c1ca5143b8686c90"} {"question" "q-316573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "69b0c4f1e8b87d115dd43be36f5eacfb20bc6694e6674c5d0161a16bf5892105"} {"question" "q-316573" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "10db4be79b372551811e9c8057554c4c907ccad3de5d46d2c1ca5143b8686c90"} {"question" "q-316573" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "34"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "10db4be79b372551811e9c8057554c4c907ccad3de5d46d2c1ca5143b8686c90"} {"question" "q-316584" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/assets/f38424364e3d4efd8ebc416974163e3eb87b3350c0c6b8ec7f5ae4ea69339824.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "10db4be79b372551811e9c8057554c4c907ccad3de5d46d2c1ca5143b8686c90"} {"question" "q-316584" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 3=6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=1\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 2=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,4\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "10db4be79b372551811e9c8057554c4c907ccad3de5d46d2c1ca5143b8686c90"} {"question" "q-316584" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "69b0c4f1e8b87d115dd43be36f5eacfb20bc6694e6674c5d0161a16bf5892105"} {"question" "q-316584" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "10db4be79b372551811e9c8057554c4c907ccad3de5d46d2c1ca5143b8686c90"} {"question" "q-316584" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "24"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/140623