egin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,4\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "10db4be79b372551811e9c8057554c4c907ccad3de5d46d2c1ca5143b8686c90"} {"question" "q-316588" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "69b0c4f1e8b87d115dd43be36f5eacfb20bc6694e6674c5d0161a16bf5892105"} {"question" "q-316588" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "10db4be79b372551811e9c8057554c4c907ccad3de5d46d2c1ca5143b8686c90"} {"question" "q-316588" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "24"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "10db4be79b372551811e9c8057554c4c907ccad3de5d46d2c1ca5143b8686c90"} {"question" "q-316612" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The triangle $D$ has vertices $(2,1),(6,1),(5,4).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "10db4be79b372551811e9c8057554c4c907ccad3de5d46d2c1ca5143b8686c90"} {"question" "q-316612" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/assets/92ee29a22baa10f4af25db8221e7d67c729f5f0f1b5e1b3c37aee7e31a92bdfb.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 3=6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=4\\cdot 1-1\\cdot (-3)=4+3=7.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,7\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =42.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "10db4be79b372551811e9c8057554c4c907ccad3de5d46d2c1ca5143b8686c90"} {"question" "q-316612" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "69b0c4f1e8b87d115dd43be36f5eacfb20bc6694e6674c5d0161a16bf5892105"} {"question" "q-316612" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "10db4be79b372551811e9c8057554c4c907ccad3de5d46d2c1ca5143b8686c90"} {"question" "q-316612" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "42"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "10db4be79b372551811e9c8057554c4c907ccad3de5d46d2c1ca5143b8686c90"} {"question" "q-9296" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The unit square $D$ has vertices $(1,0),(0,0),(0,1),(1,1).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "10db4be79b372551811e9c8057554c4c907ccad3de5d46d2c1ca5143b8686c90"} {"question" "q-9296" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/assets/3cbf4ce4422e043cedb73e9b10bba11e9cb1e64352ff182eff8aaa0046c4e8f3.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=1\\cdot 1=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=1\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 1=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,2\\,|\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "10db4be79b372551811e9c8057554c4c907ccad3de5d46d2c1ca5143b8686c90"} {"question" "q-9296" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "69b0c4f1e8b87d115dd43be36f5eacfb20bc6694e6674c5d0161a16bf5892105"} {"question" "